---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro'
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Issue a Credential"
  description="Issue and verify a W3C Verifiable Credential in under 5 minutes with the Attestto VC SDK."
  currentPath="/docs/quickstart/issue-a-credential/"
>
  <div class="docs-hero-badge">Quickstart &middot; 5 minutes</div>
  <h1>Issue a Credential</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Generate keys, issue a W3C Verifiable Credential, and verify it — all in
    under 20 lines of code. No server, no blockchain, no configuration.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="Terminal">
<Fragment set:html={`npm install <span class="c-str">@attestto-com/vc-sdk</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>The complete flow</h2>
  <p>This script creates a key pair, issues a credential, and verifies it:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="quickstart.ts">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCIssuer, VCVerifier, generateKeyPair <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-cm">// 1. Generate Ed25519 keys</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>()

<span class="c-cm">// 2. Create an issuer with your DID</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> issuer = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCIssuer</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  did: <span class="c-str">'did:web:my-org.example.com'</span>,
  privateKey: keys.privateKey,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

<span class="c-cm">// 3. Issue a credential</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'UniversityDegree'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:student.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    degree: <span class="c-str">'Computer Science'</span>,
    level: <span class="c-str">'Bachelor'</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
  expirationDate: <span class="c-str">'2030-01-01T00:00:00Z'</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Issued:'</span>, JSON.<span class="c-fn">stringify</span>(vc, <span class="c-num">null</span>, <span class="c-num">2</span>))

<span class="c-cm">// 4. Verify it</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> verifier = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCVerifier</span>()
<span class="c-kw">const</span> result = <span class="c-kw">await</span> verifier.<span class="c-fn">verifyWithKey</span>(vc, keys.publicKey, <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>, <span class="c-br">{</span>
  expectedType: <span class="c-str">'UniversityDegree'</span>,
  expectedIssuer: <span class="c-str">'did:web:my-org.example.com'</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Valid:'</span>, result.valid)     <span class="c-cm">// true</span>
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Checks:'</span>, result.checks)  <span class="c-cm">// detailed check results</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Run it</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="Terminal">
<Fragment set:html={`npx tsx quickstart.ts`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <p>You'll see the full W3C Verifiable Credential JSON with proof, followed by the verification result.</p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <p>The issued credential follows the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/" target="_blank">W3C VC Data Model v2.0</a>:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="JSON" title="Output — Verifiable Credential">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-br">{</span>
  <span class="c-attr">"@context"</span>: [<span class="c-str">"https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1"</span>],
  <span class="c-attr">"id"</span>: <span class="c-str">"urn:uuid:..."</span>,
  <span class="c-attr">"type"</span>: [<span class="c-str">"VerifiableCredential"</span>, <span class="c-str">"UniversityDegree"</span>],
  <span class="c-attr">"issuer"</span>: <span class="c-str">"did:web:my-org.example.com"</span>,
  <span class="c-attr">"issuanceDate"</span>: <span class="c-str">"2026-04-15T..."</span>,
  <span class="c-attr">"credentialSubject"</span>: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    <span class="c-attr">"id"</span>: <span class="c-str">"did:web:student.example.com"</span>,
    <span class="c-attr">"degree"</span>: <span class="c-str">"Computer Science"</span>,
    <span class="c-attr">"level"</span>: <span class="c-str">"Bachelor"</span>
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
  <span class="c-attr">"proof"</span>: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    <span class="c-attr">"type"</span>: <span class="c-str">"Ed25519Signature2020"</span>,
    <span class="c-attr">"verificationMethod"</span>: <span class="c-str">"did:web:my-org.example.com#key-1"</span>,
    <span class="c-attr">"proofValue"</span>: <span class="c-str">"..."</span>
  <span class="c-br">}</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>Zero native dependencies.</strong> The SDK uses <code>@noble/curves</code> for
    pure JavaScript Ed25519 and ES256 cryptography. Works everywhere Node.js runs — no OpenSSL, no native modules.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Key concepts</h2>
  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">DID</strong> — Decentralized Identifier. Your issuer identity. Works with any DID method (did:web, did:sns, did:key).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">VC</strong> — Verifiable Credential. A cryptographically signed claim about a subject.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Proof</strong> — The digital signature that makes the credential verifiable.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Schema Plugin</strong> — Extend the SDK with domain-specific credential types and JSON-LD contexts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><a href="/docs/credentials/schemas/">Add schema plugins</a> — use Costa Rica credential types or create your own</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/credentials/key-management/">Key management</a> — Ed25519 vs ES256, key generation, storage patterns</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/credentials/verifying/">Advanced verification</a> — DID resolvers, expiration checks, revocation</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/quickstart/add-did-login/">Add DID login</a> — use credentials for authentication</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
